# Build context for .ci/Dockerfile and .ci/Dockerfile.android.
#
# Both images copy only VERSION and scripts/ (they install dependencies;
# the source is mounted or checked out by the jobs that use them). An
# allowlist keeps the context to a few hundred KB.
#
# Without this the context is the whole working tree, which on a
# developer machine means target/ — tens of gigabytes of build artifacts
# streamed into the daemon before the first layer runs. CI never noticed
# because a fresh checkout has no target/, but it makes reproducing an
# image build locally fail with a confusing out-of-space error from
# *inside* the container.
#
# If you add a COPY to either Dockerfile, add a matching `!` line here.
*
!VERSION
!scripts
